WEBVTT

00:00:03.730 --> 00:00:05.400
Haruto!

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:06.310
Haruto!

00:00:12.700 --> 00:00:14.740
Haruto...

00:00:18.330 --> 00:00:19.280
Where's Haruto?!

00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:20.740
Where on earth did he go?!

00:00:20.740 --> 00:00:24.920
Gauche-<i>sama</i> and Droite-<i>sama</i> are currently tracing Haruto's whereabouts...

00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:35.430
<i>Have you found Haruto? Gauche?! Droite?!</i>

00:00:35.430 --> 00:00:38.760
Tch, which of those guys opened there mouth?

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:40.390
Who told Kaito?

00:00:42.930 --> 00:00:44.270
<i>Why won't you answer?!</i>

00:00:44.270 --> 00:00:46.350
<i>Answer me! Gauche! Droite!</i>

00:00:46.350 --> 00:00:49.270
Obviously because you're so damn annoying!

00:00:50.690 --> 00:00:54.360
Relax. We have confirmed Haruto's safety.

00:00:54.360 --> 00:00:55.280
Droite!

00:00:55.280 --> 00:00:58.320
<i>But he is not under our protection yet.</i>

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:02.490
<i>And Kaito, we will require your strength.</i>

00:01:02.490 --> 00:01:07.500
<i>Right now Haruto is located at
 the top of Windmill Tower in 5th Area…</i>

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:10.460
<i>...along with Yuma Tsukumo.</i>

00:01:12.340 --> 00:01:13.590
What're you talking about?

00:01:13.590 --> 00:01:15.470
You trying to call that guy here?

00:01:15.470 --> 00:01:16.930
The heck are you feeling?

00:01:16.930 --> 00:01:18.970
Have you forgotten Haruto's power?

00:01:20.760 --> 00:01:23.810
As he is now, we can't approach him.

00:01:27.230 --> 00:01:31.020
Kaito is the only one Haruto accepts from the bottom of his heart.

00:01:31.020 --> 00:01:34.820
He's the only person Haruto will listen to.

00:01:42.280 --> 00:01:43.620
<i>Windmill Tower...</i>

00:01:47.750 --> 00:01:48.420
<i>Here.</i>

00:01:51.880 --> 00:01:53.550
<i>It's called caramel.</i>

00:01:53.550 --> 00:01:56.510
<i>It's got a magical power that makes you feel better.</i>

00:01:58.630 --> 00:02:01.010
<i>Delicious...! It's really delicious!</i>

00:02:01.010 --> 00:02:03.470
<i>Haruto... I'll stay with you forever.</i>

00:02:08.480 --> 00:02:10.440
<i>Haruto!</i>

00:02:10.940 --> 00:02:13.400
<i>Haruto!!</i>

00:02:14.860 --> 00:02:16.240
<i>That place...</i>

00:02:16.240 --> 00:02:18.570
<i>And he's with Yuma Tsukumo?</i>

00:02:19.570 --> 00:02:21.450
H-Hey, Haruto!

00:02:21.450 --> 00:02:22.410
You...

00:02:22.410 --> 00:02:25.830
It seems Haruto-<i>sama</i> wanted to see me again.

00:02:27.450 --> 00:02:31.250
My mission is to destroy the Astral World.

00:02:31.250 --> 00:02:34.960
Haruto!

00:02:35.440 --> 00:02:38.110
<i>As I get closer, I stretch my hand out</i>

00:02:38.110 --> 00:02:41.160
<i>towards that shining light leading towards tomorrow</i>

00:02:41.330 --> 00:02:48.420
<i>I dream of a world that expands from my feet.</i>

00:02:52.170 --> 00:02:57.680
<i>I haven't a clue of where things like dreams and hopes are at.</i>

00:02:57.680 --> 00:03:02.180
<i>Even if I run looking for it, I still can't seem to find it.</i>

00:03:03.140 --> 00:03:08.640
<i>I wonder if I have fallen into a gap of truth and lies.</i>

00:03:08.640 --> 00:03:13.440
<i>Even so, our grand tale has yet to begin.</i>

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:19.110
<i>Let's move on towards tomorrow, 
even if our road begins to fall apart.</i>

00:03:19.110 --> 00:03:24.370
<i>I will jump forward, before all my
 strength completely drains.</i>

00:03:24.790 --> 00:03:27.250
<i>The closer I get, the further it becomes,</i>

00:03:27.370 --> 00:03:30.540
<i>that truth that I must seize.</i>

00:03:30.540 --> 00:03:35.710
<i>It's to find hope that we desire from a future unseen.</i>

00:03:35.710 --> 00:03:38.300
<i>With a heart stronger than anyone else,</i>

00:03:38.510 --> 00:03:41.470
<i>I'll learn to keep running up.</i>

00:03:41.800 --> 00:03:47.020
<i>With the strength to win any battle, 
despite just how weak I am,</i>

00:03:47.520 --> 00:03:49.520
<i>My purpose is to find,</i>

00:03:49.520 --> 00:03:52.520
<i>with these invaluable friends of mine,</i>

00:03:52.520 --> 00:03:59.320
<i>The future of the world expanding
 from my feet with my own eyes.</i>

00:04:10.140 --> 00:04:12.730
Well, it's a good thing, isn't it?

00:04:12.730 --> 00:04:16.150
That guy before seemed to know Haruto.

00:04:16.150 --> 00:04:20.900
"Number 41: Haruto's Gone!
 A New Enemy, Tron"

00:04:16.560 --> 00:04:18.230
Yeah, you're right.

00:04:18.230 --> 00:04:21.400
I'm sure he was sent by Kaito to pick him up.

00:04:26.370 --> 00:04:27.620
Kaito...

00:04:28.700 --> 00:04:34.500
<i>Brother is... always tired because of me.</i>

00:04:36.080 --> 00:04:37.080
<i>So...</i>

00:04:38.130 --> 00:04:40.250
<i>This time, I wanted to give my brother caramel.</i>

00:04:40.250 --> 00:04:43.260
<i>I wanted him to eat the caramel.</i>

00:04:43.840 --> 00:04:49.220
So he.... Kaito was really gathering Numbers for Haruto's sake.

00:04:51.640 --> 00:04:53.980
Just what the heck is going on?

00:04:53.980 --> 00:04:58.020
His reason for collecting the Numbers is...

00:05:00.780 --> 00:05:04.450
<i>My mission is to destroy the Astral World.</i>

00:05:04.450 --> 00:05:07.110
<i>Just what was that...?</i>

00:05:09.740 --> 00:05:11.160
Wh-What the heck?!

00:05:12.500 --> 00:05:13.960
It's the helicopter that took Haruto-<i>kun</i>!

00:05:17.330 --> 00:05:18.630
Y-You're...!

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:21.460
You damn brat!

00:05:21.460 --> 00:05:23.050
Where's Haruto?!

00:05:23.050 --> 00:05:24.090
What the heck?!

00:05:24.090 --> 00:05:26.800
Didn't Haruto go back home?!

00:05:26.800 --> 00:05:27.890
Say what now?!

00:05:27.890 --> 00:05:29.300
Someone came to pick him up!

00:05:29.300 --> 00:05:31.010
You didn't hear about it?!

00:05:31.010 --> 00:05:32.600
He was one of your people, wasn't he?

00:05:35.230 --> 00:05:38.190
That helicopter before had the same mark as yours!

00:05:39.150 --> 00:05:40.730
Did you hear anything about that, Droite?

00:05:43.070 --> 00:05:43.860
Yuma...

00:05:43.860 --> 00:05:49.320
No, we should be the only team out searching for Haruto.

00:05:49.320 --> 00:05:54.330
Lying right to me face, huh? You're in a bold mood today, kid! Huh?!

00:05:55.250 --> 00:05:57.870
Ow-ow, ow, ow, ow!

00:05:57.870 --> 00:05:59.040
Stop it!

00:05:59.040 --> 00:06:03.000
Hurry up and tell me where Haruto is! Otherwise...

00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:07.510
I... ain't... lyin'!

00:06:13.560 --> 00:06:15.060
I returned Haruto already!

00:06:15.060 --> 00:06:18.310
I don't got the time to fool around with you!

00:06:18.310 --> 00:06:21.650
You little bastard! The mood just got even better!

00:06:22.360 --> 00:06:23.520
You!

00:06:23.520 --> 00:06:26.320
Let go! Let go of me!

00:06:24.980 --> 00:06:26.320
Listen well.

00:06:26.320 --> 00:06:29.490
We are members of the Duel Carnival Operation Committee.

00:06:29.490 --> 00:06:34.450
If you continue to act like that, we have the right to disqualify you.

00:06:35.490 --> 00:06:36.910
Darn...

00:06:36.910 --> 00:06:39.460
If you don't want that to happen, answer honestly!

00:06:39.460 --> 00:06:41.380
Where is Haruto?

00:06:41.380 --> 00:06:42.880
Ah! That's...!

00:06:52.550 --> 00:06:53.300
Landing!

00:06:54.140 --> 00:06:56.180
Where is he?

00:06:56.180 --> 00:06:58.100
Where is Haruto?!

00:06:58.940 --> 00:06:59.440
Droite!

00:07:02.360 --> 00:07:07.400
Hey, Kaito! These guys think I'm the one who's hiding Haruto!

00:07:07.400 --> 00:07:09.530
You were hiding Haruto?

00:07:09.530 --> 00:07:14.240
No! I turned Haruto over to someone from Heartland who came to pick him up!

00:07:15.080 --> 00:07:17.240
Someone came to pick him up from Heartland?

00:07:17.240 --> 00:07:20.500
Huh? So then that means...

00:07:47.980 --> 00:07:50.950
Then what the heck is going on here?!

00:07:51.820 --> 00:07:54.120
Who... Who took Haruto?!

00:07:54.740 --> 00:07:56.160
Don't play dumb, Foolma!

00:07:56.160 --> 00:07:58.540
You were the one who kidnapped Haruto-<i>sama</i>, weren't you?!

00:07:58.540 --> 00:07:59.580
Get lost.

00:07:59.580 --> 00:08:00.790
U-Understood!

00:08:01.330 --> 00:08:04.960
You said someone from Heartland picked him up. What did they look like?

00:08:04.960 --> 00:08:05.880
Huh?

00:08:05.880 --> 00:08:08.500
I mean their characteristics! Were they male or female?!

00:08:08.500 --> 00:08:09.630
It was a man!

00:08:09.630 --> 00:08:10.670
That's all?!

00:08:10.670 --> 00:08:12.880
He was a very young man!

00:08:12.880 --> 00:08:15.890
He was in his early 20's, very skinny, and...

00:08:15.890 --> 00:08:19.020
His height was 185 cm (about 6’1).

00:08:19.020 --> 00:08:20.890
His weight was about 70 Kg (about 155-160 lbs).

00:08:20.890 --> 00:08:23.770
Right! His height was 185 cm!

00:08:23.770 --> 00:08:25.100
His weight was 70 kg!

00:08:25.100 --> 00:08:28.610
He had long hair, and his eyes were blue.

00:08:28.610 --> 00:08:33.360
He had long hair! And his eyes were... huh?
 What color were they again?

00:08:33.360 --> 00:08:35.070
Why you little...! You messing with us?!

00:08:35.070 --> 00:08:36.530
Stop it, Gauche!

00:08:36.530 --> 00:08:39.540
Shut up! I don't take orders from you!

00:08:39.540 --> 00:08:41.000
Gauche!

00:08:41.000 --> 00:08:45.670
Droite! Are you saying you believe his stupid words?!

00:08:45.670 --> 00:08:52.130
I'm not saying I believe him per say, but he doesn't seem to be lying either...

00:08:53.840 --> 00:08:55.050
Let's go, Gauche!

00:08:55.050 --> 00:08:57.390
It must be someone else who took Haruto.

00:08:57.390 --> 00:08:59.430
Tch. If you insist.

00:09:02.220 --> 00:09:03.020
Yuma!

00:09:13.280 --> 00:09:17.160
Sorry, I gave Haruto away without checking with him first...

00:09:20.410 --> 00:09:23.290
Haruto... He's sick.

00:09:24.460 --> 00:09:25.080
Sick?

00:09:28.250 --> 00:09:29.290
Wait a minute, Kaito!

00:09:30.290 --> 00:09:32.380
It's my responsibility to let Haruto go!

00:09:33.130 --> 00:09:34.670
I'm going to look for Haruto too!

00:09:37.090 --> 00:09:38.840
It's none of your business.

00:09:39.180 --> 00:09:41.890
Kaito, I promised Haruto.

00:09:42.470 --> 00:09:44.310
I swore to let him see you!

00:09:49.560 --> 00:09:50.310
Orbital.

00:09:50.900 --> 00:09:54.990
Understood! If you happen to find him, please contact us, Foolma.

00:10:08.960 --> 00:10:09.750
Kaito...

00:10:17.050 --> 00:10:21.050
I can't believe we actually gave Haruto to a stranger when he's sick.

00:10:23.640 --> 00:10:27.060
<i>Kaito, why are you collecting Numbers?</i>

00:10:27.850 --> 00:10:29.560
<i>Why are you acting like the underling of a devil?</i>

00:10:32.940 --> 00:10:36.650
<i>To save my brother, I sold my soul to the devil.</i>

00:10:38.110 --> 00:10:40.030
So Kaito collecting Numbers...

00:10:40.780 --> 00:10:42.950
...has something to do with Haruto's sickness?

00:10:44.540 --> 00:10:47.370
and what did he mean by selling his soul to the devil?

00:10:48.080 --> 00:10:50.500
Darn! What did he mean by "devil"?

00:10:50.920 --> 00:10:55.880
For now we know that Droite and Gauche are trying to find Haruto as well.

00:10:57.090 --> 00:11:01.220
Droite and Gauche were either ordered to find Haruto,

00:11:02.390 --> 00:11:06.560
or they encountered some trouble, and let Haruto slip away.

00:11:06.560 --> 00:11:09.310
They looked panicked, like they were desperately trying to cover their mistakes.

00:11:11.150 --> 00:11:11.980
So that means...

00:11:12.980 --> 00:11:15.480
Not only are those two part of the Duel Carnival operation committee,

00:11:15.940 --> 00:11:19.070
but they are also subordinates of Mr. Heartland, the main founder of this tournament.

00:11:19.610 --> 00:11:21.410
They're from Heartland?

00:11:21.990 --> 00:11:26.740
I'm afraid the reason they were searching Haruto must have something to do with Mr. Heartland.

00:11:27.450 --> 00:11:30.460
It's likely that Haruto escaped from the Heartland's security.

00:11:31.250 --> 00:11:32.370
He escaped?

00:11:32.960 --> 00:11:37.800
Then Kaito... is working under Heartland for Haruto...

00:11:38.210 --> 00:11:40.170
collecting the Numbers?

00:11:40.720 --> 00:11:42.550
In other words, the devil is...

00:11:43.590 --> 00:11:45.050
...Mr. Heartland.

00:11:57.940 --> 00:12:01.200
But... if the one who took Haruto is neither Droite or Gauche...

00:12:01.700 --> 00:12:07.200
Exactly. The problem is someone else has an eye on Haruto besides them.

00:12:08.410 --> 00:12:10.540
Who in the world are those people?

00:12:30.810 --> 00:12:33.190
Alright, let's start the ritual!

00:12:37.860 --> 00:12:38.440
<i>Where...</i>

00:12:39.150 --> 00:12:40.150
<i>Where are you, Haruto?</i>

00:12:44.740 --> 00:12:45.360
<i>Answer me!</i>

00:12:48.410 --> 00:12:49.740
<i>Haruto!</i>

00:13:09.760 --> 00:13:10.510
<i>Found you!</i>

00:13:12.930 --> 00:13:13.600
<i>Brother!</i>

00:13:16.020 --> 00:13:17.900
<i>You really are awesome, Brother!</i>

00:13:18.230 --> 00:13:21.530
<i>You always find me, no matter where I go!</i>

00:13:22.480 --> 00:13:23.150
<i>That's right!</i>

00:13:25.360 --> 00:13:26.990
I will definitely find you this time!

00:13:27.870 --> 00:13:28.820
So scream all you want!

00:13:30.080 --> 00:13:31.240
Call me!

00:13:44.970 --> 00:13:46.930
Now... it's finally here.

00:13:47.430 --> 00:13:50.350
The time has finally come for me to make Haruto's power mine!

00:14:12.910 --> 00:14:17.000
My revenge hereby starts from this moment!

00:14:17.290 --> 00:14:19.880
Just wait, Dr. Faker!

00:14:27.050 --> 00:14:29.010
<i>Ooh... that is...</i>

00:14:30.970 --> 00:14:32.850
<i>That's Astral World!</i>

00:14:33.470 --> 00:14:35.020
<i>How beautiful!</i>

00:14:35.680 --> 00:14:39.980
<i>I can feel it... I can feel... Haruto's power!</i>

00:15:03.670 --> 00:15:07.920
<i>This...this is the power I am looking for!</i>

00:15:09.010 --> 00:15:09.720
<i>Amazing...</i>

00:15:10.930 --> 00:15:11.890
<i>So wonderful!</i>

00:15:14.850 --> 00:15:16.560
Brother!

00:15:17.770 --> 00:15:19.310
The voice just now...Haruto!

00:15:22.060 --> 00:15:23.230
What happened, Astral?

00:15:23.980 --> 00:15:24.610
Haruto...

00:15:25.940 --> 00:15:26.610
Haruto is...

00:15:27.440 --> 00:15:28.690
What's wrong with Haruto?

00:15:29.280 --> 00:15:30.700
Did something happen to Haruto-<i>kun</i>?

00:15:36.990 --> 00:15:37.700
Save me!

00:15:38.500 --> 00:15:39.540
Save me, brother!

00:15:40.540 --> 00:15:41.710
Brother!

00:15:45.790 --> 00:15:47.380
There's no mistaking it. It's Haruto!

00:15:48.260 --> 00:15:49.510
Haruto is suffering!

00:15:51.260 --> 00:15:52.430
Fantastic!

00:15:52.760 --> 00:15:54.140
This power is magnificent!

00:15:58.100 --> 00:16:01.600
Haruto, give me all of your power!

00:16:02.270 --> 00:16:03.190
Brother...

00:16:03.560 --> 00:16:04.400
Brother!

00:16:07.230 --> 00:16:09.780
Brother!

00:16:11.200 --> 00:16:11.820
Haruto?

00:16:13.110 --> 00:16:14.820
Where are you? Tell me!

00:16:16.580 --> 00:16:17.870
Haruto, answer me!

00:16:18.580 --> 00:16:19.240
Brother...

00:16:20.450 --> 00:16:26.210
The moon reflected in the water outside the white castle!

00:16:30.420 --> 00:16:31.550
The moon reflected in the water...

00:16:32.050 --> 00:16:33.220
A white castle?

00:16:37.550 --> 00:16:39.770
Did Haruto really say that?

00:16:40.180 --> 00:16:42.060
Ah. That's what he said.

00:16:42.850 --> 00:16:45.810
The moon reflected in the water outside the white castle.

00:16:46.690 --> 00:16:49.820
The moon reflected in the water outside the white castle?

00:16:50.940 --> 00:16:51.860
They indicate...

00:16:54.990 --> 00:16:56.280
The moon reflected in the water...

00:16:59.330 --> 00:17:03.500
If I recall, there's an old museum no one uses around here.

00:17:05.620 --> 00:17:09.040
That's what he meant by white castle, don't you think?

00:17:10.090 --> 00:17:11.300
I see!

00:17:11.380 --> 00:17:16.890
Also, the moon reflected in the water must suggest the moonlight reflected off the lake!

00:17:17.050 --> 00:17:18.180
Alright!

00:17:18.510 --> 00:17:19.220
That's it!

00:17:19.430 --> 00:17:20.760
Now that we know the address, let's roll!

00:17:24.230 --> 00:17:25.560
Kaito! Kaito!

00:17:26.980 --> 00:17:27.650
Kaito?

00:17:34.570 --> 00:17:35.990
So Haruto is here.

00:17:36.660 --> 00:17:37.320
Haruto-<i>kun</i>.

00:17:42.910 --> 00:17:46.540
Kaito... Haruto's in there. There's no mistake!

00:17:47.870 --> 00:17:49.630
How do you know that?

00:17:50.170 --> 00:17:52.210
I know... because...!

00:17:52.840 --> 00:17:55.670
What do know?! You aren't even his brother!

00:17:56.220 --> 00:17:57.800
What do you know about Haruto?!

00:17:58.090 --> 00:18:01.310
Brother!

00:18:02.010 --> 00:18:04.310
Yuma, Haruto is in pain!

00:18:05.730 --> 00:18:09.020
Hey Kaito, this isn't the time to be arguing.

00:18:12.480 --> 00:18:15.240
They're here. They came a lot quicker than I thought.

00:18:15.900 --> 00:18:17.860
Were you followed, V?

00:18:18.450 --> 00:18:19.240
Impossible.

00:18:19.660 --> 00:18:23.740
Well, we were going to defeat them sooner or later anyhow.

00:18:23.740 --> 00:18:25.410
Not like it matters if it's a bit earlier.

00:18:26.120 --> 00:18:27.290
Then let's get going!

00:18:28.250 --> 00:18:29.250
Don't push yourself!

00:18:30.380 --> 00:18:34.050
Huh? Are you saying I can't beat them?

00:18:34.590 --> 00:18:37.880
Kaito is a formidable adversary. Don't fixate on defeating him so much.

00:18:38.550 --> 00:18:42.640
It's fine as long as we buy some time for Tron's ritual.

00:18:43.310 --> 00:18:46.020
Hmph! I don't know what'll would happen once the fight starts.

00:18:46.980 --> 00:18:48.940
I can't guarantee their lives!

00:18:50.020 --> 00:18:50.650
III.

00:18:53.190 --> 00:18:53.980
I'm counting on you.

00:18:54.820 --> 00:18:56.570
Yes, Brother V.

00:19:11.500 --> 00:19:14.500
Looks like they are inviting us.

00:19:14.920 --> 00:19:18.420
Interesting! In that case, let's rush right in!

00:19:19.420 --> 00:19:20.630
You go back!

00:19:21.430 --> 00:19:22.220
Kaito!?

00:19:23.140 --> 00:19:24.470
I can't go back!

00:19:25.600 --> 00:19:28.640
I'm the one who gave Haruto to someone else other than you.

00:19:29.430 --> 00:19:31.940
So unless I return Haruto to you safely,

00:19:32.520 --> 00:19:34.980
I ain't going back!

00:20:08.010 --> 00:20:11.230
I finally get to meet you, Kaito! I've been waiting.

00:20:18.690 --> 00:20:19.990
You're IV!

00:20:20.990 --> 00:20:21.700
You know them?

00:20:22.530 --> 00:20:22.990
Yes...

00:20:30.870 --> 00:20:33.420
Are you here to avenge your friends?

00:20:33.790 --> 00:20:35.920
Fine, I welcome the challenge anytime.

00:20:41.630 --> 00:20:43.470
Don't let your anger make you lose focus!

00:20:44.010 --> 00:20:46.300
If you are influenced by anger, your Dueling will suffer!

00:20:46.890 --> 00:20:50.770
I know, I won't use Dueling to get my revenge!

00:20:51.350 --> 00:20:53.190
Did you kidnap Haruto?

00:20:53.640 --> 00:20:54.900
Where is Haruto?!

00:20:54.940 --> 00:20:57.060
He;s still alive, so relax.

00:20:57.400 --> 00:20:58.820
For the <i>moment</i>, that is...

00:20:59.150 --> 00:20:59.980
What did you say?!

00:21:00.070 --> 00:21:02.690
But I can't give him to you yet.

00:21:03.030 --> 00:21:04.990
He's quite "occupied" at the moment, you see.

00:21:06.740 --> 00:21:09.700
If you wish to save your little brother...

00:21:11.830 --> 00:21:14.250
...do it after you defeat us.

00:21:14.250 --> 00:21:17.460
It's... a Tag Duel!

00:21:18.630 --> 00:21:21.170
Let's go! I'll bring it to 'em!

00:21:21.840 --> 00:21:25.260
I won't forgive anyone who tried to hurt Haruto!

00:21:45.400 --> 00:21:47.280
D-Gazer, set!

00:21:50.620 --> 00:21:51.700
I'll hunt...

00:21:53.580 --> 00:21:55.410
... your souls!

00:21:58.080 --> 00:22:00.000
<i>AR Vision. Link established.</i>

00:22:01.090 --> 00:22:01.750
Duel!!

00:22:02.130 --> 00:22:07.220
Brother!!

00:22:20.190 --> 00:22:23.360
<i>Someone gave me some water.</i>

00:22:23.730 --> 00:22:29.280
<i>So I was able to paint a rainbow with ease.</i>

00:22:30.410 --> 00:22:35.200
<i>I want to become someone perfect.</i>

00:22:36.000 --> 00:22:38.250
<i>But it's very difficult.</i>

00:22:39.370 --> 00:22:41.840
<i>Even with me suffering,</i>

00:22:41.960 --> 00:22:45.920
<i>I can't seem to grasp victory.</i>

00:22:46.800 --> 00:22:48.720
<i>I want to bloom!</i>

00:22:49.260 --> 00:22:53.180
<i>I must be having some kind of weird dream.</i>

00:22:53.180 --> 00:22:56.220
<i>But If I must fulfill this,</i>

00:22:56.730 --> 00:22:59.520
<i>Then I don't mind being laughed at for it.</i>

00:22:59.690 --> 00:23:06.610
<i>Since it's because your limits are decided on your own.</i>

00:23:06.900 --> 00:23:09.650
<i>I'll show it, overcoming it to tomorrow.</i>

00:23:09.910 --> 00:23:14.120
<i>Ah, I'm aiming for the big blue sky.</i>

00:23:14.330 --> 00:23:16.080
<i>For all of its glory.</i>

00:23:16.080 --> 00:23:17.870
<i>The Freesia of Desire.</i>

00:23:19.620 --> 00:23:23.250
<i>All of those countless flower petals</i>

00:23:23.460 --> 00:23:26.300
<i>They came at the expense of</i>

00:23:27.130 --> 00:23:29.880
<i>me being able to reach those heights.</i>

00:23:30.260 --> 00:23:34.300
<i>Ah, even though I lost my way today,</i>

00:23:34.470 --> 00:23:36.140
<i>I still yearn for it.</i>

00:23:36.140 --> 00:23:38.430
<i>That Freesia of Desire.</i>

00:23:41.270 --> 00:23:46.150
In order to recover Haruto, Kaito and I start a Tag Duel with IV and III.

00:23:46.730 --> 00:23:48.110
Stop it, Kaito!

00:23:50.780 --> 00:23:52.360
Why'd you do that to Yuma!?

00:23:52.860 --> 00:23:56.370
Without cooperation from him, we can't win this Duel!

00:23:56.740 --> 00:23:59.620
It's okay if you treat me as an enemy...

00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:02.540
...but I already promised Haruto!

00:24:03.250 --> 00:24:04.710
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ZeXal!

00:24:05.130 --> 00:24:07.210
"Yuma and Kaito: A Spirited Tag Duel"

00:24:07.710 --> 00:24:09.260
I'm gonna bring it to 'em!

00:24:10.720 --> 00:24:13.220
Heartland City's symbol is Mr. Heartland,

00:24:13.260 --> 00:24:15.930
so "Heartland's Mr. Heartland" is pretty tedious!

00:24:16.010 --> 00:24:18.890
There are many repetitive matters in this world.

00:24:19.100 --> 00:24:20.600
Like soup pot, salsa sauce, etc.

00:24:21.140 --> 00:24:22.560
Hope King Hope!
 (Literal for "Aspiring Emperor - Hope)

00:24:22.940 --> 00:24:24.020
Don't say it like that.
